# Written by the release workflow's harness check, and by anyone reproducing it.
harness.json

# The engine's build copies the root CAPABILITY.md in beside its dist, so the
# published tarball carries the list that VERSIONING.md tells consumers to diff.
# The root copy is the source; this one is an artefact.
packages/formula-engine/CAPABILITY.md

# oracle harness intermediates — fixtures are regenerated, not committed
tools/oracle/build/
tools/oracle/out/

# Scale fixtures are generated by tools/verify/scale.mjs, not source.
apps/demo/public/scale-*.xlsx

# Eval fixtures are generated by eval/build.py, and the recalculated copies by
# LibreOffice. Both are reproducible; the model scripts are the source.
eval/build/

# The real-data corpus is other people's business workbooks: budgets, board
# packs, a business plan, shared for a technical purpose and not for
# publication. None of it is committed — not the files, not the harness that
# reads them, not the report, not the rule file. Earlier revisions of this
# project kept the report and the scripts, on the reasoning that counts and
# timings carry nothing confidential; that was true of the numbers and false of
# the *filenames*, which name the companies. Once the repository went public the
# whole directory came out, history included.
#
# What survives is in the README: the aggregates, and the bugs the corpus found.
# The two harnesses a reader can actually rerun — the oracle and the synthetic
# corpus — are both in this repository, which is the point of having three.
eval/Real data/
eval/real/
